  "explanation": "The 4 chord (Ab) with a D in it. D is the #11, a raised 4th above Ab. It already belongs to Eb major, so it shimmers and still sounds like home's family.",
  "why": "It is a colour you reach for often, in Eb and in Db.",
  "try": "Keep the loop going. On the Ab bar, move your top finger between C and D: C is the plain chord, D is the shimmer. Then try D over the Eb bar too, where it is the major 7th.",
